# oracle: create_atoms with random molecule orientations, then velocity loop geom: the orientations take sin and cos
# of random angles (C library values), the positions set the loop geom seeds, so a one-ulp difference changes velocities
# Measured with native LAMMPS: thermo 8.9e-16, per-atom 8.4e-15 relative with the glibc sin/cos (src/engine/libm.ts);
# with Math.sin / Math.cos the step-5 temperature was off by 3e-5 relative (one-ulp orientations changed the seeds).
# oracle-inputs: w32gcmc_dimer.mol
units		lj
atom_style	molecular
lattice		sc 0.08
region		box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box	1 box
molecule	dimer w32gcmc_dimer.mol
create_atoms	0 box mol dimer 734594
mass		1 1.0
pair_style	lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff	1 1 1.0 1.0
velocity	all create 0.5 87287 loop geom
fix		1 all nve
timestep	0.002
thermo_style	custom step temp pe ke
thermo_modify	format float %.15g
thermo		5
run		20
